# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# **`!.env.example` does not match a nested path** — B-212, 2026-08-07. A
# negation without a directory only rescues the pattern at the repository
# root, so `infra/.env.prod-local.example` was silently swallowed by
# `.env.*` and the commit that added it appeared to succeed. **`make up`
# would have told every lane to copy a file the repository does not ship**,
# which is the §2 defect inside the fix for the §2 defect. Caught by
# `git check-ignore -v` before the push rather than by a lane.
!.env*.example
!infra/.env*.example

